---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Sebastian Correa-Gallego"
  description="Sebastian Correa-Gallego — Bachelor of Science in Biology, Universidad EAFIT. Microbial ecology, community assembly along environmental gradients, and cellular resource allocation."
  ogType="profile"
>
  <div class="container">

    <header class="intro">
      <img
        src="/assets/profile.jpg"
        alt="Portrait of Sebastian Correa-Gallego"
        class="intro__photo"
        width="118"
        height="118"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <h1 class="intro__name">Sebastian Correa-Gallego</h1>
      <p class="intro__subtitle">Bachelor of Science in Biology</p>
    </header>

    <section id="about" class="block">
      <h2 class="heading reveal">About</h2>
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <p>
          Evolution and ecology are not subfields of biology — they are its organizing logic,
          present from the emergence of cellular complexity to the structure of communities in
          extreme environments. My research interests sit at this intersection: I am drawn to
          microbial systems as tractable windows into how life assembles, persists, and
          transforms under ecological and energetic constraint. This includes questions about
          community organization along environmental gradients, the physiological and molecular
          strategies — including cellular resource allocation — that underlie ecological success,
          and the eco-evolutionary dynamics that connect cellular function to community-level
          patterns. I am also interested in the quantitative and computational frameworks that
          make these questions formally tractable, and in connecting field-based inquiry with
          analytical rigor across biological scales.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="research" class="block">
      <h2 class="heading reveal">Research</h2>

      <article class="card reveal">
        <span class="card__meta">Undergraduate thesis · Universidad EAFIT</span>
        <h3 class="card__title card__title--italic">
          Cultivable Microbial Community Structure Along a Light Gradient in a Tropical
          Volcaniclastic Cave
        </h3>
        <p class="card__sub">Sole author · Advisor: Prof. Nicolás Pinel Peláez</p>
        <p class="card__desc">
          A field-to-lab study characterizing how cultivable microbial community structure
          shifts across a light-defined environmental gradient in a subterranean system.
        </p>
        <a class="card__link" href="https://hdl.handle.net/10784/38213" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Read the thesis — EAFIT institutional repository →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="card reveal">
        <span class="card__meta">Ongoing collaboration · Purdue University</span>
        <h3 class="card__title">Proteome allocation in osmotrophic yeasts under carbon limitation</h3>
        <p class="card__sub">ECSO Lab · Visiting Student Intern, 2025–2026</p>
        <p class="card__desc">
          Continuing work on how osmotrophic yeasts allocate proteomic resources under carbon
          limitation, connecting cellular physiology to ecological strategy. A manuscript is in
          preparation; details will appear here once published.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section id="presentations" class="block">
      <h2 class="heading reveal">Presentations</h2>
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__row">
            <span class="entry__title">Research proposal presentation</span>
            <span class="entry__date">2024</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry__sub">2nd Symposium of Biology, Universidad EAFIT · <em>Awarded second place</em></p>
        </div>
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__row">
            <span class="entry__title">Oral presentation</span>
            <span class="entry__date">2024</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry__sub">XXIII Encuentro Departamental de Semilleros de Investigación, RedCOLSI, Antioquia</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="honors" class="block">
      <h2 class="heading reveal">Honors &amp; Recognition</h2>
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__row">
            <span class="entry__title">Fully funded visiting internship</span>
            <span class="entry__date">2025</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry__sub">Fundación Fraternidad Medellín — UREP-C Program</p>
        </div>
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__row">
            <span class="entry__title">Undergraduate scholarship</span>
            <span class="entry__date">2022</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry__sub">Comfama and Fundación Fraternidad Medellín</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="record" class="block">
      <h2 class="heading reveal">Academic Record</h2>
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__row">
            <span class="entry__title">B.Sc. in Biology</span>
            <span class="entry__date">2022–2026</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry__sub">Universidad EAFIT · GPA 4.44 / 5.00</p>
        </div>
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__row">
            <span class="entry__title">Visiting Student Intern</span>
            <span class="entry__date">Aug 2025 – Jan 2026</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry__sub">ECSO Lab, Department of Biological Sciences, Purdue University</p>
        </div>
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__row">
            <span class="entry__title">Undergraduate Thesis Researcher</span>
            <span class="entry__date">2024–2026</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry__sub">Universidad EAFIT · Advisor: Prof. Nicolás Pinel Peláez</p>
        </div>
        <div class="entry">
          <div class="entry__row">
            <span class="entry__title">Student Director, Microbiology &amp; Astrobiology Group (SIAB)</span>
            <span class="entry__date">Oct 2023 – May 2025</span>
          </div>
          <p class="entry__sub">Universidad EAFIT · affiliated with GEBI</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="skills" class="block">
      <h2 class="heading reveal">Technical Profile</h2>
      <div class="prose prose--muted reveal">
        <p>
          My training spans cultivation-based microbiology, environmental sampling, microscopy,
          and morphotype characterization from fieldwork in subterranean systems, together with
          cell physiology and continuous-culture workflows developed at Purdue.
        </p>
        <p>
          I complement laboratory and field practice with quantitative analysis in R and Python,
          data visualization, and reproducible, literate workflows — aiming to connect
          field-based inquiry with analytical rigor across biological scales.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</Base>
